      "name": "Local & Regional Move Operations",
      "description": "Local and regional move operations from survey to walkthrough. The operation chain runs survey, quote, pack, load, transport, unload, place, reassemble, unpack, and a final walkthrough. Survey runs through the quote form — Short (Quick Quote) default and Detailed Project, switching in place with the From, To and What's moving inputs preserved — or through the free film-only video walkthrough survey room, where the customer films and a person makes the estimate; nothing is auto-priced. The published scope is homes and businesses across the Shenandoah Valley and the Eastern Panhandle: packing and unpacking, loading and unloading, priced by the job, not by the hour, at one flat rate agreed in writing before move day. Load order runs heavy pieces low and first, room-staged boxes next, fragile items secured on top, everything strapped; placement is room by room by label, with reassembly of standard furniture. Transport follows the I-81, I-66 and I-70 corridors as the route fits. Both bases dispatch across the region — Winchester serves the Valley side, Martinsburg the Eastern Panhandle side, with overlap at Moorefield — and the quote form settles which crew and route fit the move. Where a move includes a high-mass piece of 1,500 to 3,500 lbs, that item moves under SIR Structural Integrity Relocation with the KIM-GS Protocol and L/360 floor-deflection analysis, as part of the same flat-rate move. Home depth cross-references the residential category, business depth the office category, and moves beyond the region the long-distance category — cross-references are links, never duplicated claims.",
